### GCP Project Creation 
1. Create a GCP Project 

2. GCP Project list 
    ```bash
    $ gcloud projects list
    PROJECT_ID                  NAME                        PROJECT_NUMBER  ENVIRONMENT
    weather-project-prod-511603  weather-project-prod        
    ```

3. Sync gcloud
    ```bash
    $ gcloud auth login
    Your current project is [XYZ Project].  You can change this setting by running:
    $ gcloud config set project PROJECT_ID

4. Set your project:
    ```bash
    $ gcloud config set project weather-project-prod-51160
    ```
5. Verify:
    ```bash
    $ gcloud config get-value project
    weather-project-prod-51160
    ```
5. Delete a project (Only for reference, don't use it)
  ```bash
  gcloud projects delete weather-project-prod-51160
  ```

### Docker & Artifact
1. Install docker 

2. Configure Docker authentication
   $ gcloud auth configure-docker asia-south2-docker.pkg.dev
    {
    "credHelpers": {
        "us-central1-docker.pkg.dev": "gcloud",
        "asia-south2-docker.pkg.dev": "gcloud"
    }
    }
    Adding credentials for: asia-south2-docker.pkg.dev
    gcloud credential helpers already registered correctly


3. Create Artifact Registry repository 
        [GCP > Artifact Registry > https://console.cloud.google.com/artifacts]

    $ gcloud artifacts repositories create ecommerce-nodejs-app-repo \
        --repository-format=docker \
        --location=asia-south2 \
        --description="Microservices Nodejs"

    Created repository [ecommerce-nodejs-app-repo].

    Verify
    $ gcloud artifacts repositories list --location=asia-south2    

    ARTIFACT_REGISTRY
    REPOSITORY: ecommerce-nodejs-app-repo
    FORMAT: DOCKER
    MODE: STANDARD_REPOSITORY
    DESCRIPTION: Microservices Nodejs
    LOCATION: asia-south2

    Ref: asia-south2-docker.pkg.dev/weather-project-prod-511603/ecommerce-nodejs-app-repo
    
4. Build the Node.js image from indivisual repo

    docker build -f apps/order-service/Dockerfile -t order-service:1.0 .
    docker build -f apps/user-service/Dockerfile -t user-service:1.0 .
    docker build -f apps/product-service/Dockerfile -t product-service:1.0 .

